 <longdesc><para unique="1091454">Rotates the bits of source operand right by the count value specified in imm8 without affecting arithmetic flags. <anchor id="+334466"/>The result is written to the destination operand.</para>
  <para unique="1091455">This instruction is not supported in real mode and virtual-8086 mode. The operand size is always 32 bits if not in 64-bit mode. In 64-bit mode operand size 64 requires VEX.W1. VEX.W1 is ignored in non-64-bit modes. An attempt to execute this instruction with VEX.L not equal to 0 will cause #UD.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <programlisting>IF (OperandSize = 32)
	y := imm8 AND 1FH;
	DEST := (SRC &gt;&gt; y) | (SRC &lt;&lt; (32-y));
ELSEIF (OperandSize = 64)
	y := imm8 AND 3FH;
	DEST := (SRC &gt;&gt; y) | (SRC &lt;&lt; (64-y));
FI;</programlisting>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1091465">Flags Affected</title>
   <programlisting>None.</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
